Subject: [PATCH] feat: delete sessions from picker with Ctrl+D

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Delete the selected session directly from the session picker.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1004-personal-feature-configure-session-picker-default-filter.patch

Patch intent:
Add Ctrl+D to delete the selected session from the session picker without a
confirmation prompt. Remove the backing local snapshot and journal or the
external transcript, then remove the row from the open picker.

Why it exists:
Users need a fast way to remove obsolete sessions while reviewing their
session history. This intentionally provides no undo or confirmation step.

Upstream integration points:
SessionPicker::handle_overlay_key routes Ctrl+D to deletion. Session storage
paths provide the local snapshot and journal paths, and the picker cache is
invalidated so a later /resume does not show a deleted session. Server-group
sessions are removed from their group in all_server_groups.

Update guidance:
Preserve the unmodified d debug toggle. Keep deletion scoped to the selected
entry and remove every storage file owned by that supported session source.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-tui ctrl_d_deletes_the_selected_session_without_closing_the_picker --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui ctrl_d_deletes_external --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui ctrl_d_deletes_session_with_missing --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui deleted_session_invalidates --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui ctrl_d_deletes_session_from_server_group --lib
